From 9838ea7a478cea71f4ea2ab53eb5101f5f62d177 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 04:53:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] analysis: cell identity consistency detector
 (T-OR-059)

CellConsistencyAnalyzer (default off) flags a cell inconsistent with itself
across one recording: the same E-UTRAN cell identity (from SIB1) advertised
with two different tracking area codes, or -- correlating the most recent
serving SIB1 with an ML1 serving measurement (T-OR-058) -- measured on two
different physical cell ids. A real cell has one fixed (identity, TAC, PCI);
a mismatch can be identifier cloning or rotation by a false base station.

Corroborative and Low, off by default pending T-OR-061 calibration. State is
per recording (first value seen per cell identity). The PCI half uses the
RRC_IDLE ML1 serving log, so it covers idle-mode; connected-mode PCI is T-OR-117.

Privacy: compares cell-identity / TAC bit patterns and PCI values but never
puts any identifier in an event -- it reports only that a mismatch occurred.

Test vectors are SIB1 PDUs encoded with the reference Python pycrate and
decoded through telcom_parser: same cell identity with two TACs (fires), with
one TAC (quiet), two different cell identities (quiet); and ML1 serving
measurements giving the same cell identity two PCIs (fires) / one PCI (quiet),
plus a measurement before any SIB1 (quiet).

